{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "00WO", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-representable-sheaves}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:73c7b96fa2001d7a797a5196183e9c2b2aa75895b269f315d4d01be098ba16bd", "source_text": "Representable sheaves", "source_text_hash": "sha256:709e9d9e920b2ff9dd56e41ed3bffefb7534939f96cf5dd47e19506d794ecd04", "unit_id": "tag:00WO:title"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00WO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-canonical-topology}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c0f0df21fd5bf03ac80850077883ce0cc992127aed19159a6abeeb0df016bd72", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4b63de76e60200fba58549bc56403496befcdcf267f80ef2c97c6dfe6bdceaa2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a category. The canonical topology is\nthe finest topology such that all representable presheaves\nare sheaves (it is formally defined in\nDefinition <REF_0001> but we will not\nneed this).\nThis topology is not always the topology associated to the\nstructure of a site on <MATH_0002>.\nWe will give a collection of coverings that generates this topology\nin case <MATH_0003> has fibered products. First we give\nthe following general definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:012e3f1c54fe735c609645fa5a29d0ddd726e8ad419ef3564c57ac8dae6a465e", "unit_id": "tag:00WO:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00WO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$U_i \\to U$", "MATH_0004": "$X\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(U, X) \\ar[r]\n&\n\\prod\\nolimits_{i \\in I} \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(U_i, X)\n\\ar@<1ex>[r] \\ar@<-1ex>[r]\n&\n\\prod\\nolimits_{(i, j) \\in I^2} \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(U_i \\times_U U_j, X)\n}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0007": "$V \\to U$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{U_i \\times_U V \\to V\\}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-definition-representable-morphism}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-universal-effective-epimorphisms}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a668624e6b0d31328f4c913337a39035047fe5b63d43585e8af5f1f979a27292", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b9539243e692ce61ea92e32ab77d6128777e8a844983f7235f7f42922a2dfdcd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category. We say that a family <MATH_0002>\nis an <TEXTITOPEN_0001>effective epimorphism<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if all the morphisms <MATH_0003> are\nrepresentable (see\nCategories, Definition <REF_0001>),\nand for any <MATH_0004> the sequence\n<MATH_0005>\nis an equalizer diagram. We say that a family <MATH_0006> is a\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>universal effective epimorphism<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if for any morphism <MATH_0007>\nthe base change <MATH_0008> is an effective epimorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ddcdff47a73377d2a25ba0a0b75eb6fe374c5aa8f65f717dca735e92ba524df7", "unit_id": "tag:00WP:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00WO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-site}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sets-lemma-coverings-site}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2c51efac6cbb691d7cdbe11f357625c9fc6c3e8de5f6bbae3a6c54be8728c86b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0b19a8ba7f4da802cbca062394fe6b864483adc3b17a84630d7332403c99855c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe class of families which are universal effective epimorphisms\nsatisfies the axioms of Definition <REF_0001>.\nIf <MATH_0001> has fibre products, then the associated topology is\nthe canonical topology. (In this case, to get a site argue as in Sets,\nLemma <REF_0002>.)\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nConversely, suppose that <MATH_0002> is a site such that\nall representable presheaves are sheaves. Then clearly, all\ncoverings are universal effective epimorphisms.\nThus the following definition is the ``correct'' one in the\nsetting of sites.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b92c0865a71cb7f90f08c51c436a7efaaf39331861c78d3762f60fb845c5a77d", "unit_id": "tag:00WO:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00WO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-weaker-than-canonical}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2c51efac6cbb691d7cdbe11f357625c9fc6c3e8de5f6bbae3a6c54be8728c86b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:34703c450d9996e090c05ff586a61fb0483c4a0ea1ba216e483c0f6177e5136b", "source_text": "We say that the topology on a site <MATH_0001> is\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>weaker than the canonical topology<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, or that the topology is\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>subcanonical<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if all the coverings\nof <MATH_0002> are universal effective epimorphisms.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:103da711777b34d6b521170b59f18c5dbfad67965a9197e0f1e5d0463b5a982b", "unit_id": "tag:00WQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00WO", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2521cbedca7c68de46a07980e5629dd732047ee43e705b95fdf3da20d77f50ac", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nA representable sheaf is a representable presheaf which is also a\nsheaf. Since it is perhaps better to avoid this terminology when the\ntopology is not subcanonical, we only define it formally in that case.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cb1cc3f9c506c051d00606b85694e597503ecd239760e368dc5d309caf331405", "unit_id": "tag:00WO:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00WO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$h$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$h_U$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0008": "$h_U$", "MATH_0009": "$U$", "MATH_0010": "$\\underline{U}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-section-opposite}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-representable-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:669f6d82c8db61948c9197cb0a05cb5e76ecf077f16efee3fcd4a710852b00a6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1e9458e5b94c1156fbabd10f2015c9abc6192e01066373426f46c6b3ef2ecdcd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site whose topology is subcanonical.\nThe Yoneda embedding <MATH_0002> (see\nCategories, Section <REF_0001>)\npresents <MATH_0003> as a full subcategory of the\ncategory of sheaves of <MATH_0004>. In this case\nwe call sheaves of the form <MATH_0005> with <MATH_0006>\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>representable sheaves<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> on <MATH_0007>.\nNotation: Sometimes, the representable sheaf <MATH_0008> associated to <MATH_0009> is\ndenoted <TEXTITOPEN_0002><MATH_0010><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:547d99059d09ff849b1f932d63d9e45975b936025ebfe515fe30688bb275c2e1", "unit_id": "tag:00WR:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00WO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})}(h_U, \\mathcal{F}) = \\mathcal{F}(U)\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$h_U$", "MATH_0004": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-map-representable-into-sheaf}\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})}(h_U^\\#, \\mathcal{F}) =\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})}(h_U, \\mathcal{F}) =\n\\mathcal{F}(U)\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\#$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-map-representable-into-presheaf}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{equation-map-representable-into-presheaf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fcdfe389e2b48e8b9d3dba6eca1f6a3da885577fc116b85a6a17b527e5a73b63", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:585bee84b4aebeef649ef17ad12304b8f6e3ae26cd956e24d7d79fe54a1ce086", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that we have in the situation of the definition\n<MATH_0001>\nfor every sheaf <MATH_0002>, since it holds for presheaves, see\n(<REF_0001>). In general the\npresheaves <MATH_0003> are not sheaves and to get a sheaf you have to\nsheafify them. In this case we still have\n<MATH_0004>\nfor every sheaf <MATH_0005>. Namely, the first equality holds\nby the adjointness property of <MATH_0006> and the second is\n(<REF_0002>).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:416acf4ab66519ef53d9dd99ab8ef8caa10b24cf7dc136f40eafdb0450e9a225", "unit_id": "tag:00WO:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00WO", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nCoverings become surjective after sheafification.\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\coprod\\nolimits_{i \\in I} h_{U_i} \\to h_U\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-covering-surjective-after-sheafification}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6e2c947262f5a30d071a4dab4048371cbe00a1f6e7f893cf0e699bda6d0437ba", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c3e57a423c99e23da34687cc84cc3d5618ee0789a97262a3712c05bdb7e5caa3", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a site. If\n<MATH_0002> is a covering of the site\n<MATH_0003>, then the morphism of presheaves of sets\n<MATH_0004>\nbecomes surjective after sheafification.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:660ac698064bd21615f8d957dc6269fcf01581664f5914c4e69c28f6fdbdee52", "unit_id": "tag:00WT:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00WO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\coprod\\nolimits_{i \\in I} h_{U_i}^\\# \\to h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$h_U^\\# \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$s \\in \\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Mor(h_U^\\#, \\mathcal{F})\n\\to \\prod_i \\Mor(h_{U_i}^\\#, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-mono-epi-sheaves}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dfd04747de2d841b20bde51ec3f97f8161b013b9de37a92670bc6161e91e6a8e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:141116e6db69fcf455e4dcad844400096114e128f0e08e78f790fec52ae3ddfb", "source_text": "By Lemma <REF_0001> above we have to show that\n<MATH_0001>\nis an epimorphism. Let <MATH_0002> be a sheaf of sets.\nA morphism <MATH_0003>\ncorresponds to a section <MATH_0004>.\nHence the injectivity of <MATH_0005> follows\ndirectly from the sheaf property of <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dc4312dd694e3989f6eb24e6667792724dff00300fecb57fe9d99cc2af036c40", "unit_id": "tag:00WT:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00WO", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2521cbedca7c68de46a07980e5629dd732047ee43e705b95fdf3da20d77f50ac", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe next lemma says, in the case the topology is weaker than the\ncanonical topology, that every sheaf is made up out of\nrepresentable sheaves in a way.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:94378bb5e2fc764a245db9ba182f1af0391ecea71a1f104229972acae161a275", "unit_id": "tag:00WO:prose-0005"}
